/**
 * PROVIDER REGISTRY WHITELIST
 * ------------------------------------------------------------------
 * Ordered list of provider registry classes to activate for this app.
 *
 * A provider in CitOmni is typically a package Boot\Registry class that may
 * contribute config, service maps, and dispatch maps for the active runtime mode.
 *
 * What a provider may contribute:
 *   - Common config overlays via: CFG_COMMON
 *   - Mode config overlays via:   CFG_HTTP / CFG_CLI
 *   - Common service maps via:    MAP_COMMON
 *   - Mode service maps via:      MAP_HTTP / MAP_CLI
 *   - HTTP route maps via:        ROUTES_HTTP
 *   - CLI command maps via:       COMMANDS_CLI
 *
 * There is no ROUTES_COMMON or COMMANDS_COMMON. Dispatch remains mode-specific.
 *
 * Config merge model (last wins):
 *   1) Vendor mode baseline: CFG_HTTP or CFG_CLI from the active runtime package
 *   2) Provider #1 CFG_COMMON, then provider #1 CFG_HTTP or CFG_CLI
 *   3) Provider #2 CFG_COMMON, then provider #2 CFG_HTTP or CFG_CLI
 *   4) App common base: /config/citomni_cfg.php
 *   5) App mode base: /config/citomni_http_cfg.php or /config/citomni_cli_cfg.php
 *   6) App common env overlay: /config/citomni_cfg.{ENV}.php
 *   7) App mode env overlay: /config/citomni_http_cfg.{ENV}.php or /config/citomni_cli_cfg.{ENV}.php
 *
 * Service precedence model (left wins via PHP array union +):
 *   - App mode services win over app common services.
 *   - App common services win over provider services.
 *   - Later providers win over earlier providers when service ids collide.
 *   - Within one provider, MAP_HTTP/MAP_CLI wins over MAP_COMMON for the active mode.
 *   - Vendor mode baseline has the lowest precedence.
 *
 * Dispatch merge model (last wins):
 *   - HTTP routes: vendor ROUTES_HTTP -> provider ROUTES_HTTP -> app routes -> app env routes.
 *   - CLI commands: vendor COMMANDS_CLI -> provider COMMANDS_CLI -> app commands -> app env commands.
 *
 * Requirements:
 *   - Only plain FQCN strings belong here.
 *   - No arrays, no closures, no logic, no side effects.
 *   - Provider classes must be autoloadable through Composer.
 *   - Missing or invalid provider classes fail fast by design.
 *
 * Policy:
 *   - Keep this file intentional and ordered.
 *   - Only list provider registry classes you actually want active in this app.
 *   - Do not put app config, service definitions, routes, or commands here.
 *   - Prefer a short, explicit list over speculative enablement.
 *
 * Notes:
 *   - This file is app-owned after installation.
 *   - Provider order matters.
 *   - Shared package defaults belong in provider CFG_COMMON/MAP_COMMON.
 *   - The vendor baseline is supplied by the selected runtime package: citomni/http or citomni/cli.
 */
return [

	/*
	|--------------------------------------------------------------------------
	| Example: Infrastructure package
	|--------------------------------------------------------------------------
	| Common low-level services such as db, log, mail, txt, and related cfg.
	*/
	// \CitOmni\Infrastructure\Boot\Registry::class,

	/*
	|--------------------------------------------------------------------------
	| Example: Authentication package
	|--------------------------------------------------------------------------
	| Login, register, member area, and related auth wiring for apps that use it.
	*/
	// \CitOmni\Authenticate\Boot\Registry::class,

	/*
	|--------------------------------------------------------------------------
	| Example: Admin package
	|--------------------------------------------------------------------------
	| Admin routes, dashboards, and related backend wiring for apps that use it.
	*/
	// \CitOmni\Admin\Boot\Registry::class,

	/*
	|--------------------------------------------------------------------------
	| Example: App provider
	|--------------------------------------------------------------------------
	| App-specific config, services, routes, and commands collected in your own registry.
	*/
	// \App\Boot\Registry::class,

];
